# Licence for the datasets in this directory

The calculation records, processed results and reference values under `data/`
are licensed under the **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International**
licence (CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may share and adapt them for any purpose, including commercially, provided
you give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate if changes were
made.

The source code in this repository is licensed separately, under the MIT
licence; see the `LICENSE` file at the repository root.

## Third-party data redistributed here

`reference/motta_h10_obc_sto6g.json` is derived from the Simons Collaboration
hydrogen-chain benchmark and is redistributed under its own CC BY 4.0 licence:

> M. Motta *et al.* (Simons Collaboration on the Many-Electron Problem),
> *Phys. Rev. X* **7**, 031059 (2017), doi:10.1103/PhysRevX.7.031059.
> Data: https://github.com/simonsfoundation/hydrogen-benchmark-PRX, CC BY 4.0.

That attribution is also carried inside the file itself.

`reference/n2_ccpvdz_external.json` contains numerical values transcribed from
the published tables of three papers, each cited inside the file. Individual
numerical results are facts rather than creative works, no licence is claimed
over them, and they are re-derivable by anyone running the same calculation.
The papers themselves are not redistributed.

## Provenance metadata

Every record carries the software versions, host and platform it was produced
on, so that a result can be traced to the machine that generated it. The
hostname is that of a personal workstation and is retained deliberately: it is
what makes the provenance chain complete.
